im not sure as to all the options that are available (hence this issue..). Its not really that clear from reading the code either.
I know that `show ip route summary` and `show ip route json` are available. The json option apparently puts a large load on the CPU which we should probably put a warning on in the command help.

The relevant code snippet / file is:

sonic-utilities/show/main.py: 
```
@ip.command()
@click.argument('args', metavar='[IPADDRESS] [vrf <vrf_name>] [...]', nargs=-1, required=False)
@click.option('--display', '-d', 'display', default=None, show_default=False, type=str, help='all|frontend')
@click.option('--namespace', '-n', 'namespace', default=None, type=str, show_default=False, help='Namespace name or all')
@click.option('--verbose', is_flag=True, help="Enable verbose output")
def route(args, namespace, display, verbose):
    """Show IP (IPv4) routing table"""
    # Call common handler to handle the show ip route cmd
    bgp_common.show_routes(args, namespace, display, verbose, "ip")
```

where bgp_common.show_routes() is defined in  sonic-utilities/show/bgp_common.py
